# Force www to non-www canonical host
# This is in addition to Netlify's automatic domain handling so that
# the redirect is explicit, documented, and Google receives a clear
# permanent (301) signal to consolidate the canonical on non-www.
https://www.scroofing.co.uk/* https://scroofing.co.uk/:splat 301!

# Site-wide rewrite: any URL without a trailing slash serves the same content
# as the slashed version (no 301 redirect, just a rewrite to status 200).
#
# Why: Astro pages declare their canonical URL as the no-trailing-slash path
# (e.g. <link rel="canonical" href="https://scroofing.co.uk/areas/widcombe">),
# but Netlify's "Pretty URLs" feature redirects the no-slash URL to the
# slashed URL with HTTP 301. The slashed page is then served, but its
# declared canonical points elsewhere, which makes Google flag the slashed
# page as "Alternate page with proper canonical tag" and de-index it.
#
# By rewriting (not redirecting) the no-slash URL to the slashed version
# with status 200, both URLs serve the same 200 content with no redirect
# chain. Google can index either URL cleanly; the canonical mismatch goes
# away.
#
# This rule does NOT affect URLs that already end in a slash — they fall
# through to Netlify's normal static file serving.
#   /areas/widcombe  ->  /areas/widcombe/   (200, no redirect)
#   /about           ->  /about/            (200, no redirect)
#   /                ->  /                  (untouched)
/*  /:splat/   200
